      "problem": "Consider a circle with center $O$ and radius $r=14,$ and the point $B$ that lies in the same plane as the circle. Which of the following conditions might be true if it's known that the point $B$ lies outside the circle?",
      "worked_solution": "We will sketch the situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182550/assets/60056e6bc44989185f3707ba013bb81d440b8a7060e5c754608e8c5977db687e.png)\n\nSince $B$ lies outside the circle, the distance between $B$ and the center $O$ of the circle must be greater than the radius. Therefore, we must have\n\n$$\nOB>r=14.\n$$\n\nAmong the given options, only $OB=15$ satisfies the above inequality.",
